---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageTitle from '../components/PageTitle.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Destination from '../components/Destination.astro';
---
<Base title="Explore — Breanna & Eric">
  <PageTitle title="Explore" />
  <Section>
    <p>If you’re already making the trip to Italy, you may want to stay a little longer. Whether you’re hoping for museums and long lunches, mountain trails, or a few days by the sea, these are a few places we think are worth building into your trip.</p>
  </Section>

  <Destination eyebrow="For art, food & wandering" name="Florence" stay="Suggested stay: 2–3 nights"
    favorites="Duomo • Uffizi • Accademia • Oltrarno • Boboli Gardens • Wine windows" artLabel="Watercolor: Florence" artSrc="images/placeholders/art-florence.jpg">
    <p>Florence is an easy place to spend a few extra days before or after the wedding. Wander through the historic center, see the Renaissance art, cross the Arno into Oltrarno, and leave plenty of time for long meals, wine, and getting a little lost.</p>
    <p slot="note"><em>If the Uffizi or Accademia is high on your list, it is worth planning museum tickets ahead of time.</em></p>
  </Destination>

  <Destination eyebrow="For mountains & adventure" name="The Dolomites" artFirst
    stay="Suggested stay: 3–4 nights in Ortisei / Val Gardena" favorites="Seceda • Alpe di Siusi • Mountain hiking • Rifugios • Via ferrata" artLabel="Watercolor: Dolomites" artSrc="images/placeholders/art-dolomites.jpg">
    <p>If you would rather trade museums for mountain air, base yourself in one of the alpine villages and spend a few days hiking, riding the lifts into the mountains, stopping at rifugios, and taking in a completely different side of Italy.</p>
    <p>Cortina d’Ampezzo is another great base, especially if places like Cinque Torri, Tre Cime, or via ferrata are high on your list.</p>
    <p slot="note"><em>The Dolomites take more travel time than our other suggestions, so we would plan at least a few nights. Lift and transportation schedules are seasonal, so check current operations before booking your itinerary.</em></p>
  </Destination>

  <Destination eyebrow="For coast & sunshine" name="Sorrento" stay="Suggested stay: 3–4 nights"
    favorites="Capri • Pompeii • Positano/Amalfi Coast • Marina Grande" artLabel="Watercolor: Sorrento" artSrc="images/placeholders/art-sorrento.jpg">
    <p>For a few days by the water, Sorrento lets you slow down in town, with the Bay of Naples and the Amalfi Coast close by when you want them.</p>
    <p slot="note"><em>Sorrento is farther from Tuscany, so think of it as a true trip extension rather than a quick add-on after the wedding.</em></p>
  </Destination>
</Base>
